        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "White wholecloth quilted crib cover with finely woven linen top and more coarsely woven linen back. Densely quilted pattern of intertwining scrolls and leaves or feathers and small globes made with yellow silk thread, possibly back stitched. Monograms incorporated into quilted design include \"ICN\", \"HC\", and \"MN\". Edges are bounded with white warp-faced plain woven silk. Stained."@en ;
